 NIC-3, second attempt. `nicsitting.img` flew 2026-08-14, answered NIC-1 and
 NIC-2, and then painted `NIC-3 below writes to the part` and stopped. The next
 expression was `e1000-init d`, so `e1000-init` was entered and did not return.

 THIS PROBE DOES NOT CALL `e1000-init`. It performs that function's own
 sequence, in its own order, out of its own primitives, with a row painted
 BEFORE every step that can loop. The last row on the glass therefore names the
 loop that did not return, which is the whole question (L-STATES).

 EVERY STEP THAT RETURNS ALSO PRINTS ITS DURATION, and that is the second half
 of the design. A step that never returns and a step that takes four minutes
 look identical on a photograph of a stalled screen, and they are different
 findings with different fixes. `e1000-await-link` alone is 4,000,000 polls of
 an MMIO register; NIC-2 measured metal at 2.50x the bed for a RAM-side poll,
 and an MMIO read crosses the PCH, so a long-but-finite spin is a live
 hypothesis and this is what would distinguish it.

 THE DRIVER IS UNCHANGED. Every call below is `E1000e`'s own, in `e1000-init`'s
 own order, so a different outcome cannot be blamed on a different sequence.
 The one thing reproduced rather than called is the BODY of `e1000-reset` and
 of `e1000-init-after-reset`: those are the two functions whose interiors need
 rows, and their bodies are transcribed operation for operation below. That is
 the same licence `AsdeStageProbe` took on 2026-08-13 when it split the reset
 into its five MMIO operations, and for the same reason.

 WHAT IS BANKED BEFORE THE FIRST WRITE. The touch, RCTL/TCTL and the ring
 registers, exactly as `nicsitting` painted them, so the arrival state is
 comparable with 2026-08-14 row for row. If those differ from that flight, the
 board did not arrive the way it did last time and nothing below is comparable
 either -- that is why they are re-read rather than assumed answered.

 We say:

Section: Marker Files

  nip-name : Integer -> Integer
  nip-name (buf) =
   let a = poke-byte buf 0 78
   in let b = poke-byte buf 1 73
   in let c = poke-byte buf 2 67
   in let d = poke-byte buf 3 51
   in let p1 = poke-byte buf 4 32
   in let p2 = poke-byte buf 5 32
   in let p3 = poke-byte buf 6 32
   in let p4 = poke-byte buf 7 32
   in let t = poke-byte buf 8 84
   in let x = poke-byte buf 9 88
   in poke-byte buf 10 84

  nip-bytes : Integer, Text, Integer -> Integer
  nip-bytes (buf) (s) (i) =
   if i >= text-length s then i
   else let b = poke-byte buf i (to-unicode (char-code (char-at s i)))
   in nip-bytes buf s (i + 1)

  nip-mark : GfatMount, Text -> [Device.Port] Boolean
  nip-mark (m) (body) =
   if (m.gm-ok) == False then False
   else let nb = alloc-zeroed 16 16
   in let nm = nip-name nb
   in let n = text-length body
   in let buf = alloc-zeroed 512 64
   in let w = nip-bytes buf body 0
   in gfat-write-file (m.gm-vol) nb buf n

  nip-stage-name : Integer -> Text
  nip-stage-name (s) =
   if s == gfat-stage-hdr then "GPT header read failed"
   else if s == gfat-stage-sig then "no EFI PART signature"
   else if s == gfat-stage-ents then "entry array read failed"
   else if s == gfat-stage-guid then "no ESP GUID in the entry array"
   else if s == gfat-stage-bpb then "BPB sector read failed"
   else if s == gfat-stage-bps then "bytes-per-sector not 512"
   else if s == gfat-stage-ok then "ok"
   else "not asked"

  nip-bank-line : GfatMount, Boolean -> Text
  nip-bank-line (m) (wrote) =
   if m.gm-ok then "bank live, NIC3.TXT written=" & (if wrote then "y" else "n")
   else "no bank, mount stage " & show (xdiag-get gfat-cell-stage)
        & " (" & nip-stage-name (xdiag-get gfat-cell-stage)
        & ") -- the rows below are the reading"

Section: Rows

  nrow : Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer, Integer, Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  nrow (base) (stride) (font) (y) (scale) (s) (col) (w) =
   let lines = gop-draw-text-wrap base stride font 40 y s col scale w
   in y + lines * 16 * scale + 6

  col-read : Integer = 9474192
  col-good : Integer = 3394611
  col-warn : Integer = 16755200
  col-head : Integer = 65535
  col-step : Integer = 16777088

Section: Arrival State, re-read as the comparability control

 THE ARRIVAL ROWS ARE COMPRESSED TO TWO LINES ON PURPOSE. Every line spent
 above the steps is a line the steps do not get, and at the ASUS's scale 2 the
 step rows are what the flight is for. The 2026-08-14 values are NOT printed
 beside them: a photograph does not need the comparison, the doc has it, and
 the four numbers below are what gets compared against that entry by eye.

  nip-arrival-1 : Integer -> Text
  nip-arrival-1 (mmio) =
   let r = e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-rctl
   in let t = e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-tctl
   in "arrival RCTL=" & show r & " EN=" & na-yn (bit-and r e1000-rctl-en)
     & " TCTL=" & show t & " EN=" & na-yn (bit-and t e1000-tctl-en)

  nip-arrival-2 : Integer, Integer -> Text
  nip-arrival-2 (mmio) (hz) =
   "arrival RDBAL=" & show (e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-rdbal)
     & " RDLEN=" & show (e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-rdlen)
     & " RDH=" & show (e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-rdh)
     & " RDT=" & show (e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-rdt)
     & " hpet=" & show hz

Section: Durations

 A step's cost in microseconds, from the HPET, so a slow step reads as a number
 rather than as a stall. hpet-hz is printed once above; if it is 0 or absurd
 every duration below it is void and the row says so.

  nip-us : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  nip-us (t0) (t1) (rate) = if rate <= 0 then (0 - 1) else (t1 - t0) * 1000000 / rate

 ONE LINE PER STEP, REPAINTED IN PLACE, and the reason is the glass rather than
 tidiness. Twelve steps with a separate entering row and result row is
 twenty-four lines; the bed paints at scale 1 and the ASUS at scale 2, so what
 fits here overflows there, and `OperatorsManual` already records the scale-2
 probe rows as the measured clipping surface. `nip-enter` paints ENTERING at y
 and does NOT advance. `nip-ret` blanks that same y and paints the result over
 it. So a step that returns costs one line and a step that HANGS leaves its own
 ENTERING line as the last thing on the screen, which is the reading.

  nip-line-h : Integer -> Integer
  nip-line-h (scale) = 16 * scale + 6

  nip-enter : Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer, Integer, Text, Integer -> Integer
  nip-enter (base) (stride) (font) (y) (scale) (s) (w) =
   let l = gop-draw-text-wrap base stride font 40 y s col-step scale w
   in y

  nip-ret : Integer, Integer, CbfFont, Integer, Integer, Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  nip-ret (base) (stride) (font) (y) (scale) (s) (col) (w) =
   let clr = gop-fill-rect base stride 0 y w (nip-line-h scale) 1710638
   in let l = gop-draw-text-wrap base stride font 40 y s col scale w
   in y + nip-line-h scale

  nip-done : Text, Integer, Integer -> Text
  nip-done (what) (us) (extra) =
   what & " ret " & show extra & " in " & show us & "us"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Device.Port, Device.Mmio] Integer
  opening =
   let base = boot-fb-base 0
   in let w = boot-fb-w 0
   in let h = boot-fb-h 0
   in let stride = boot-fb-stride 0
   in let font = cbf-init
   in let scale = if w >= 1024 then 2 else 1
   in act
    ri <- runtime-init 0
    att <- usb-attach
    let bg = gop-fill-rect base stride 0 0 w h 1710638
    in let y0 = nrow base stride font 40 scale "NIC INIT PROBE -- last row names the loop that hung" col-head w
    in act
      m <- gfat-mount-esp
      m0 <- nip-mark m "nic init probe, rows on the glass"
      let y1 = nrow base stride font y0 scale (nip-bank-line m m0) (if m.gm-ok then col-read else col-warn) w
      in let scan = pci-scan-all
      in let yend = when e1000-find scan
       is None -> nrow base stride font y1 scale "NO ELIGIBLE INTEL PART FOUND -- nothing below can run" col-warn w
       is Just (d) ->
         if na-eligible d == False then nrow base stride font y1 scale (na-reject-line d) col-warn w
         else let y2 = nrow base stride font y1 scale ("eligible at " & show (d.pci-bus) & ":" & show (d.pci-dev) & "." & show (d.pci-func) & " verdict=" & na-verdict-text (e1000-bar-verdict (na-bar-of d))) col-read w
         in let mmio = na-mmio-of d
         in let t = na-touch mmio
         in let started = hpet-start
         in let hz = hpet-ticks-per-second
         in let y4 = nrow base stride font y2 scale (nip-arrival-1 mmio) col-read w
         in let y7 = nrow base stride font y4 scale (nip-arrival-2 mmio hz) col-read w

         in let e1 = pci-enable-device d

         in let y8 = nip-enter base stride font y7 scale "s1 ENTERING imc+ctrl+RST writes" w
         in let a1 = e1000-write mmio e1000-reg-imc #FFFFFFFF
         in let ctrl0 = e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-ctrl
         in let a2 = e1000-write mmio e1000-reg-ctrl (bit-or ctrl0 e1000-ctrl-rst)
         in let y8b = nip-ret base stride font y8 scale ("s1 pcien=" & show e1 & " ctrl=" & show ctrl0 & " (RST discarded here)") col-read w

         in let y9 = nip-enter base stride font y8b scale "s2 ENTERING e1000-await-reset fuel 1000000" w
         in let r0 = hpet-ticks
         in let settled = e1000-await-reset mmio 0
         in let r1 = hpet-ticks
         in let y9b = nip-ret base stride font y9 scale (nip-done "s2 await-reset" (nip-us r0 r1 hz) settled) col-good w

         in let ya = nip-enter base stride font y9b scale "s3 ENTERING e1000-settle-mdio fuel 200000" w
         in let s0 = hpet-ticks
         in let waited = e1000-settle-mdio mmio
         in let s1 = hpet-ticks
         in let yab = nip-ret base stride font ya scale (nip-done "s3 settle-mdio" (nip-us s0 s1 hz) waited) col-good w

         in let a3 = e1000-write mmio e1000-reg-imc #FFFFFFFF
         in let a4 = e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-icr

         in let yb = nip-enter base stride font yab scale "s4 ENTERING e1000-quiesce RCTL=0 TCTL=0 +10ms" w
         in let q0 = hpet-ticks
         in let quiet = e1000-quiesce mmio
         in let q1 = hpet-ticks
         in let ybb = nip-ret base stride font yb scale (nip-done "s4 quiesce" (nip-us q0 q1 hz) quiet) col-good w

         in let yc = nip-enter base stride font ybb scale "s5 ENTERING ring alloc + zero" w
         in let g0 = hpet-ticks
         in let rx-ring = e1000-alloc-aligned (e1000-rx-count * e1000-desc-size) 16
         in let tx-ring = e1000-alloc-aligned (e1000-tx-count * e1000-desc-size) 16
         in let rx-bufs = e1000-alloc-aligned (e1000-rx-count * e1000-buf-size) 16
         in let tx-bufs = e1000-alloc-aligned (e1000-tx-count * e1000-buf-size) 16
         in let ctrl-blk = e1000-alloc-aligned e1000-cb-size 8
         in let cb-clear = e1000-zero-words ctrl-blk (e1000-cb-size / 4) 0
         in let g1 = hpet-ticks
         in let ycb = nip-ret base stride font yc scale (nip-done "s5 alloc" (nip-us g0 g1 hz) 0) col-good w

         in let yd = nip-enter base stride font ycb scale "s6 ENTERING e1000-clear-mta" w
         in let c0 = hpet-ticks
         in let mta = e1000-clear-mta mmio 0
         in let c1 = hpet-ticks
         in let ydb = nip-ret base stride font yd scale (nip-done "s6 clear-mta" (nip-us c0 c1 hz) mta) col-good w

         in let mac-ok = e1000-mac-present mmio
         in let mac = if mac-ok then e1000-read-mac mmio else []
         in let dev = E1000Device { e-mmio = mmio, e-rx-ring = rx-ring,
                                    e-tx-ring = tx-ring, e-rx-bufs = rx-bufs,
                                    e-tx-bufs = tx-bufs, e-ctrl-blk = ctrl-blk,
                                    e-present = True, e-mac = mac,
                                    e-mac-valid = mac-ok, e-pch = 0, e-ulp = 0 }

         in let ye = nip-enter base stride font ydb scale "s7 ENTERING e1000-setup-rx (enables the receiver)" w
         in let x0 = hpet-ticks
         in let rx = e1000-setup-rx dev
         in let x1 = hpet-ticks
         in let yeb = nip-ret base stride font ye scale (nip-done "s7 setup-rx" (nip-us x0 x1 hz) rx & " macok=" & (if mac-ok then "y" else "n")) col-good w

         in let yf = nip-enter base stride font yeb scale "s8 ENTERING e1000-setup-tx" w
         in let z0 = hpet-ticks
         in let tx = e1000-setup-tx dev
         in let z1 = hpet-ticks
         in let yfb = nip-ret base stride font yf scale (nip-done "s8 setup-tx" (nip-us z0 z1 hz) tx) col-good w

         in let yg = nip-enter base stride font yfb scale "s9 ENTERING e1000-phy-bring-up (MDIO)" w
         in let p0 = hpet-ticks
         in let phy = e1000-phy-bring-up mmio
         in let p1 = hpet-ticks
         in let ygb = nip-ret base stride font yg scale (nip-done "s9 phy-bring-up" (nip-us p0 p1 hz) phy) col-good w

         in let ctrl1 = e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-ctrl
         in let slu = e1000-write mmio e1000-reg-ctrl (bit-and (bit-or ctrl1 e1000-ctrl-slu) e1000-clear-asde)
         in let yh = nip-enter base stride font ygb scale "s10 ENTERING e1000-await-link fuel 4000000 MMIO reads" w
         in let l0 = hpet-ticks
         in let link = e1000-await-link mmio 0
         in let l1 = hpet-ticks
         in let yhb = nip-ret base stride font yh scale (nip-done "s10 await-link" (nip-us l0 l1 hz) link) (if link == 1 then col-good else col-warn) w

         in nrow base stride font yhb scale ("INIT COMPLETE RDH=" & show (e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-rdh) & " RDT=" & show (e1000-read mmio e1000-reg-rdt) & " -- photograph, then F12") col-head w
      in shot-wait base w h stride font (att.ua-kbd)
    end
   end

